  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nQuiet weather continues through mid week, allowing time for areas to \ndry out some from last week's flooding event. A few Flood Warnings \nremain in effect for portions of Turkey Creek and the Big Blue River \nin Saline and Gage counties through Monday night or Tuesday.\n\nHigh pressure sits over the Four Corners Region the next several \ndays with northwest flow over the Great Plains today. Expect a \npleasant afternoon with highs in the 70s and fairly light winds. \nBreezy conditions are expected tomorrow, with gusts up to 25-30mph. \n\nA warm front passing to the north brings some warmer air into the \nregion for Tuesday, with expected highs topping out in the mid-70s \nto low 80s. Slightly cooler weather returns Wednesday and Thursday \nwith temps slipping back into the 70s.",
